# Prismoid - deployment config. Copy to deploy/.env (chmod 600) and fill in.
# Every value here is a URL or a secret; the architecture never changes, only these (ADR-012).
# Every ${VAR:?} in compose.prod.yaml maps to a required line here - a missing one fails
# `docker compose config`, not the first user.

# ── identity: the three public hostnames ride one domain ──
# app.DOMAIN (web) · api.DOMAIN (API) · s3.DOMAIN (presigned downloads). DNS-only records, no
# CDN proxy - SSE and ACME want a straight path. ACME_EMAIL gets Let's Encrypt expiry mail.
DOMAIN=prismoid.example.com
ACME_EMAIL=you@example.com
# Public URLs derived from DOMAIN (bake-time for the SPA, CORS for the API, presign-time for
# downloads). These must be what a BROWSER reaches, never in-compose service names.
API_PUBLIC_URL=https://api.prismoid.example.com
WEB_ORIGIN=https://app.prismoid.example.com
# The operator console's origin (the separate admin application). Optional: leave unset and
# neither CORS nor anything else knows about a console. See DEPLOY.md, "The operator console".
ADMIN_ORIGIN=https://admin.prismoid.example.com
S3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT=https://s3.prismoid.example.com

# ── the muscle: at least one model provider (or point the gateway at a self-hosted vLLM/Ollama) ──
# XAI rides the OpenAI-compatible gateway provider (ADR-024) - optional, like the rest.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
XAI_API_KEY=

# ── secrets: generate each once, on the box; they must survive every redeploy ──
# Required, with no fallback in compose.prod.yaml: an empty one fails `docker compose config`.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=          # openssl rand -hex 24
MINIO_USER=prismoid
MINIO_PASSWORD=             # openssl rand -hex 24
SANDBAR_TOKEN=              # openssl rand -hex 32
# Ed25519 seed (base64, 32 bytes) - the worker signs verification reports, the API verifies.
# Losing/rotating it invalidates every prior report's signature check.
SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=        # openssl rand -base64 32
# Fernet key (urlsafe base64, 32 bytes) - connector OAuth tokens at rest. COMMA-SEPARATED to
# rotate: first key encrypts, all decrypt; bump CONNECTORS_KEY_ID alongside.
CONNECTORS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=  # python3 -c "import base64,os;print(base64.urlsafe_b64encode(os.urandom(32)).decode())"
CONNECTORS_KEY_ID=v1

# ── outbound email (ADR-031): reset codes and security notices ──
# The API REFUSES to boot with PRISMOID_ENV=prod unless the backend is smtp - the console
# backend prints password-reset codes into `docker logs`. Any SMTP relay works; e.g. Resend is
# host smtp.resend.com, port 587, username `resend`, password = the API key.
EMAIL_BACKEND=smtp
EMAIL_FROM=Prismoid <no-reply@prismoid.example.com>
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USERNAME=
SMTP_PASSWORD=

# ── the screen (ADR-065): the live view of a task's Machine, and who drives its browser ──
# The API REFUSES to boot with PRISMOID_ENV=prod while computer use is on
# (PRISMOID_COMPUTER_USE_ENABLED=true in the backend's environment) unless this key is set: it
# signs the browser's screen tickets and sandbar's display tickets, so every API replica (and
# sandbar, by its public half) must share it. REQUIRED: the stack runs Machines and the screen on,
# and compose refuses to start without it and SANDBAR_DISPLAY_KEYS. Format <kid>:<base64 of a 32-byte Ed25519 seed>;
# a malformed key fails every boot. Generate once, on the box: echo "s1:$(openssl rand -base64 32)"
SCREEN_SIGNING_KEY=
# Its public half, for sandbar's display route (a sandbar Machine's live screen): sandbar verifies
# the API's display tickets and can never mint one. REQUIRED. Print it on the box from the key alone
# (POSIX sh + openssl; sandbar/docs/api.md has the uv form):
#   KEY="$SCREEN_SIGNING_KEY"; echo "${KEY%%:*}:$({ printf '\060\056\002\001\000\060\005\006\003\053\145\160\004\042\004\040'; printf %s "${KEY#*:}" | base64 -d; } | openssl pkey -inform DER -pubout -outform DER | tail -c 32 | base64)"
SANDBAR_DISPLAY_KEYS=
# true (default): the API and the worker give a sandbar Machine a screen. false: a sandbar Machine
# has none - "This Machine has no live screen yet." - never a screen that keeps starting.
SANDBAR_SCREEN=true
# true (default): computer use is on - a browser or shell ask seats the computer and the API serves
# the screen. false is the kill switch (the rollback): browser asks fall to the other lanes and the
# screen answers "off"; Machines still run files work.
COMPUTER_USE=true

# ── observability: empty = telemetry is a silent no-op; set the token and it all lights up ──
LOGFIRE_TOKEN=
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
# stdout is JSON log records in prod (ADR-101); console prints every span instead
PRISMOID_LOG_FORMAT=
PRISMOID_LOG_LEVEL=info

# ── the object store: self-hosted MinIO (default) or any managed S3 provider ──
# Self-hosted: keep COMPOSE_PROFILES=minio and leave the S3_* lines unset - the compose
# defaults point at the minio container and S3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT is https://s3.DOMAIN via Caddy.
# Managed (DO Spaces / R2 / a hyperscaler bucket): empty COMPOSE_PROFILES (minio never
# starts), set the four S3_* values + unique bucket names, point S3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT at the
# provider's public origin, and select the s3-vhost-less ingress with CADDYFILE.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=minio
# Managed mode note: compose interpolates ${MINIO_PASSWORD:?} even in the profile-disabled
# minio service, so a Spaces deployment keeps the guard satisfied with an explicit marker:
# MINIO_PASSWORD=unused-minio-profile-disabled
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com
# S3_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3_SECRET_KEY=
# S3_ARTIFACT_BUCKET=prismoid-artifacts
# S3_SNAPSHOT_BUCKET=prismoid-snapshots
# S3_SKILL_BUCKET=prismoid-skills
# CADDYFILE=./Caddyfile.managed-s3

# ── the sandbox rootfs image sandbard launches per frame ──
# First run: prismoid-frame:prod (docker build -t prismoid-frame:prod backend/prismoid/ai/frames/image).
# deploy/deploy.sh <sha> builds every image on the box from the checked-out sha and pins this
# (and BACKEND_IMAGE/WEB_IMAGE/WEB_ADMIN_IMAGE/SANDBAR_IMAGE/GIT_SHA) to that sha's local tags.
FRAME_IMAGE=prismoid-frame:prod
# The browser profile's image, layered on FRAME_IMAGE (just sandbar-browser-image builds it by hand:
# docker build -t prismoid-frame-browser:prod --build-arg BASE_IMAGE=prismoid-frame:prod
# backend/prismoid/ai/frames/image_browser). deploy.sh builds and pins it on every deploy.
FRAME_BROWSER_IMAGE=prismoid-frame-browser:prod
# sandbard runs as an unprivileged user and reaches the Docker Engine through the socket's group.
# REQUIRED. deploy.sh pins it on every deploy and refuses a value that is not the socket's group;
# a hand-run compose needs it set: getent group docker | cut -d: -f3
DOCKER_GID=

# ── web search (ADR-047): no engine, no `web.search` tool for a task ──
# Each setting is the one line of its name below: to turn search on, fill those lines in.
# Option 1, a keyed engine (brave, tavily, exa, perplexity, parallel; the engines and the grammar
# are in backend/.env.example): PRISMOID_SEARCH_ENGINES names it and PRISMOID_SEARCH_KEYS gives its key,
# for Brave `brave` and `brave=<your key>`.
# Option 2, SearXNG on this box (no published port, no account): PRISMOID_SEARCH_ENGINES is `searxng`,
# PRISMOID_SEARCH_URLS is `searxng=http://searxng:8080`, and SEARXNG_SECRET, REQUIRED with it, is the
# output of `openssl rand -hex 32`. deploy.sh then starts it under the compose `search` profile.
# A hand-run compose needs `search` in COMPOSE_PROFILES above (`minio,search`), never
# `--profile search`: a profile flag replaces that list and leaves the object store off.
# PRISMOID_SEARCH_PRICES_PER_1K and PRISMOID_SEARCH_MODELS are optional (provider-native engines only).
PRISMOID_SEARCH_ENGINES=
PRISMOID_SEARCH_KEYS=
PRISMOID_SEARCH_URLS=
SEARXNG_SECRET=
PRISMOID_SEARCH_PRICES_PER_1K=
PRISMOID_SEARCH_MODELS=

# ── knobs with correct defaults; uncomment only to override ──
# FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS=*       # Caddy is the only route in; conf.py sanctions * for that case
# CADDY_EXTRA_GLOBAL=local_certs   # VM dry-runs only: self-signed CA instead of Let's Encrypt
# GIT_SHA=dev                 # written by deploy.sh on every deploy
